{
  "description": "Shared date cases for setValue / set_value and sheet[...] writes of Date (JS) and date / datetime / time (Python), and getDate / get_date reads. Each row: id; direction (write | read); date1904 (bool); input; expect {js, py} (a surface absent from expect does not run the row); optional only (surfaces that run the row). write input.kind: date {year, month, day}; datetime {year, month, day, hour, minute, second, subsecond {js_ms, py_us}}; time {hour, minute, second, subsecond {py_us}}; aware_datetime (a tzinfo-carrying Python datetime; utc_offset_minutes); timedelta {days}; invalid_date (JS Invalid Date); decimal {value} (Python Decimal as text); instant {iso} (JS Date parsed from an ISO-8601 UTC instant; only its UTC components count, whatever the process time zone is). write effective_format: general (a new cell, so the date format is applied) | custom (the cell already has a non-General number format) | row_style | column_style (a non-General format inherited from the row or column XF); only general applies a format. write expect: {serial, format, format_id} (format null = the cell's format is left untouched; format is the en-US code that builtin_num_fmt_id_for_en_us_code maps to format_id) or {error, layer}; serials are compared with a relative tolerance of 1e-12. read input: {serial} (a numeric cell; a string stands for NaN / Infinity / -Infinity) or {cell: blank | text | bool | error}. read expect: {date: {year..second, millisecond (js) | microsecond (py)}}, {value: null} for an empty cell, or {error, layer}. layer 1 = rejected inside the binding (RangeError / TypeError / ValueError); layer 2 = InvalidArgument from the engine. A 1900-system serial is the Excel serial (1900-02-29 does not exist as a Date / date, so no row writes it).",
  "cases": [
